+ * Surya (Poco X3 NFC, SM7150): staged Adreno 618 bring-up, off by default.
+ * Boot-arg sweetgpu=N selects one of these bounded stages:
+ *   1  read-only GCC/GPUCC gate and status report;
+ *   2  CX/GMU clocks, read-only SMMU report and GMU TCM read/write check;
+ *   3  load the stock a618_gmu.bin and cold-boot the GMU;
+ *   4  set up GMU memory/SMMU and complete the legacy HFI startup;
+ *   5  request the lowest common SM7150 GPU level (180 MHz), enable SPTPRAC,
+ *      inspect the powered GPU core, then return the GPU to slumber;
+ *   6  stage 5 plus signed a615_zap PAS authentication using the Surya carveout.
  *
- * The MMIO bases and gate checks follow the user-provided live FDT and the
- * pinned SM7150 mainline DTS. This first Surya GPU step deliberately only
- * reads ABL's current state. Do not reuse the Beryllium Adreno 630 write
- * stages: Surya has different GCC AXI, PDC, GMU chip ID, HFI votes and ZAP
- * firmware. Only sweetgpu=1 is accepted here; higher values log and return
- * before any MMIO mapping. The probe is therefore useful for collecting the
- * first hardware log without enabling clocks, changing power domains, or
- * touching GPU memory.
+ * Stages 2-6 write hardware state and must be run in order with logs reviewed
